            "review_title": "Review at India Gate Restaurant - Sapa Branch",
            "review_text": "Jason Fumes\nChingford, United Kingdom10 contributions\n0\nHorrible Experience\nMay 2026 • Friends\nFirst of all when we walked in they didn’t even acknowledge us to seat us at a table, then when we actually sat at a table they said it’s reversed ! After we sat at another table they only went & repeated themselves to us. Once we had sat down he asked what drinks we want but we didn’t see the drinks untill we had finished the starters… we had asked 3 different people for our drinks ! We asked for a glass but they brang us paper cups like it’s an absolute joke ! We asked for ice and they didn’t have any ice.. we complained to the manager & it took him exactly 4 minutes to find us 2 glasses… once the food arrived I asked the gentleman for a knife but he said we don’t do knife’s we only do folks & spoons ? I wish I could make this up but I can’t it was the most horrendous curry experience I’ve ever had. The onion baji’s were cut up like onion pieces, the chicken tikka masala was extremely spicy as if I asked for a Vindaloo curry which I didn’t ! They treated us like we were getting a takeaway and I’m sure they would get better service.\nWOULD NOT RECOMMEND\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten May 29, 2026",
